  "instructions": [
    {
      "primary_message": "Preheat oven to 425°F. ",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Peel shallots. Trim the ends, making sure to keep the shallots whole. \n\n",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Preheat a large ovenproof skillet over medium-high heat. ",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Once the skillet is hot, add butter and swirl to coat the bottom. Add shallots, arrange in a single layer, then season with salt and pepper. Cook, turning occasionally, until golden brown, 10-12 minutes. \n\n",
      "secondary_message": "¼ cup butter, unsalted\n¾ tsp salt\n¼ tsp black pepper"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Meanwhile, wash and dry the fresh produce. \n\n",
      "secondary_message": "½ small pkg fresh thyme\n¼ small pkg chives"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Thinly slice chili peppers into rings; seed and remove ribs with a spoon to reduce spice level. (Be careful with chilis; do not touch your eyes and ensure you wash your hands after handling or wear gloves while preparing.) ",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Slide thyme leaves off the stems; discard the stems.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "When the shallots are golden brown, add chili pepper, thyme, water, vinegar, and sugar to the skillet; gently stir to combine and bring to a boil. Once boiling, remove from heat. \n\n",
      "secondary_message": "¼ cup apple cider vinegar\n2 tbsp brown sugar"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Place skillet in the oven and roast, turning shallots halfway through, until sauce has reduced to a glaze-like consistency and a knife can easily pierce shallots, 40-45 minutes. Remove from oven.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Meanwhile, chop chives into small pieces. \n\n",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Transfer shallots to a serving dish, then pour glaze on top and sprinkle with chives. Enjoy!\n\n",
      "secondary_message": null
    }
  ],
